                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "23e9c8bf-c3de-3042-9f75-14396b6c2b0f",
                        "entry_id": "1110ceb4-dc21-3bc0-9a8c-e045c5abd2f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To weep over; weep for; weep about; deplore; lament."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "050ad289-66db-4494-b9b3-2de3a57e6403",
                                "sense_id": "23e9c8bf-c3de-3042-9f75-14396b6c2b0f",
                                "text": "c. 1593, Michael Drayton, The Shepheards Garland, The Second Eglog, 2nd edition,\nWith Nymphs and shepheards yearly moane\nHis timeless death beweeping.\nIn telling that my hart alone\nHath his last will in keeping."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9a97397-6240-406b-ab49-6c850a0ee610",
                                "sense_id": "23e9c8bf-c3de-3042-9f75-14396b6c2b0f",
                                "text": "When, in disgrace with fortune and men’s eyes,\nI all alone beweep my outcast state"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "819647d7-004a-4df9-a59b-07f82098069d",
                                "sense_id": "23e9c8bf-c3de-3042-9f75-14396b6c2b0f",
                                "text": "Let Gods, men, brutes, beweep him, plants and stones.\nSo shall she know your loss was dear indeed.\nAnd bend her heart, and give you Balder back."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                        "entry_id": "1110ceb4-dc21-3bc0-9a8c-e045c5abd2f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To weep."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3983c92-dbeb-47c9-a977-80834897bccf",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "Fast by her style doth wery labour stand./ Pale fere also, and sorrow all bewept"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "922d361f-9018-4fd7-aa19-ddeb3f0e873e",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "Child! Arline! wilt thou? darest thou heap A stain thine after life will beweep, On these hairs by thee and sorrow bleach'd On this hear dishonour never reach'd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f550108-7679-4f8d-a86a-b6caba665c72",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "And therefore saith Job to God, ' Suffer, Lord, that I may a while bewail and beweep, ere I go without returning to the dark land, covered with the darkness of death ; to the land of misease and of darkness, whereas is the shadow of death; whereas is no order nor ordinance, but grisly dread that ever shall last.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02eb6a4d-07d2-4fa4-bf6b-64007378e4bb",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "Cinnamongirl: I am in disgrace in my fellow maidens' eyes and I do beweep alone in my outcast state."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b55560a-ee87-4439-a4a5-b1bc1e3f3b27",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "Anyway, not wishing to speak too much of myself- for 'my Auschwitz adolescence to whom beweep?/ Since my Belsen boyhood sent all to sleep'- I'll just take a single incident from my childhood to show how, 'Midnight's children' fashion, I too changed history by Giving Saddam Hussein the idea for biological weapons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0713aaa5-8807-44b3-bfa2-2fea6be32b8b",
                                "sense_id": "dfbd71ec-a7c9-3901-ac9a-5cc959060487",
                                "text": "How could I condemn a name that honours so many of my friends for whose distance or loss I now beweep?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
